# Cloudflare Pages redirects.
# Reference: https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/redirects/
#
# Goal: send the CF-assigned *.pages.dev and *.workers.dev hostnames to the
# canonical custom domain so the duplicate hostnames don't surface in
# Cloudflare Security Center insights.
#
# Caveats (verify post-deploy with `curl -sI`):
#   - Full-URL sources (scheme + host) are NOT in the CF Pages supported-
#     features table; "Domain-level redirects" is listed as unsupported.
#     If CF Pages silently drops these lines, fall back to disabling
#     pages.dev subdomain access in the project settings.
#   - The trailing `!` is Netlify force-flag syntax and is not documented
#     for CF Pages; on Pages, redirects always apply regardless of asset
#     match, so the flag would be redundant even if it parses. Do NOT
#     cargo-cult `!` into path-only rules added later.
#   - `*` in the source captures everything; `:splat` reuses it in the
#     destination. That pairing is correct per the docs.
https://aragornwang-com.pages.dev/* https://aragornwang.com/:splat 301!
https://aragornwang-com.wangaragorn.workers.dev/* https://aragornwang.com/:splat 301!
